    "1": {
      "note": "Cantonese school life uses verb-object compounds. <strong>duk6 syu1</strong> (讀書) literally 'read book' = study generally. <strong>soeng5 tong4</strong> (上堂) literally 'ascend class' = attend a lesson. <strong>haau2 si3</strong> (考試) = take an exam. Two words for 'knowing': <em>sik1</em> (識) = know how to / be able to (skills), versus <em>zi1</em> (知, knowing a fact). 'I can speak Cantonese' uses <em>sik1</em>; 'I know that' uses <em>zi1</em>.",
